**Improving test coverage with integration**

I’m planning to add a realistic release integration test using a distinct folder and git worktree setup to simulate the actual PowerShell workflow. This will help catch test gaps beyond existing replay tests, especially addressing JSON parsing edge cases and verifying the usage of `SITE_DATA`. I want to make sure the tests are runnable, repeatable, and correctly detect any false failures.
**Coordinating PowerShell and browser tests**

I’m setting up a fresh run directory and using a PowerShell runner alongside Node spawn to build a standalone PowerShell script that runs core and replay commands concurrently without resource conflicts. I plan to add negative mutation tests targeting date validation and reinforce test assurance by explicitly checking for all passes. This setup avoids overcomplicating tests while ensuring no code weakening and supports continuous integration checks for unstaged changes.
